# .graphifyignore
#
# Was a whitelist — `*` then `!src/` + `!src/**`. Current graphify applies the
# catch-all first and prunes the tree before the negations can rescue anything,
# from every scan root, so `detect()` returned **0 files** for the whole repo and
# `graphify update` happily wrote a 0-node graph over graph.json (2026-09-03).
#
# Same intent — index the frontend source — expressed as exclusions, which the
# ignore engine cannot reinterpret. The scan root stays the repo root so
# `graphify update` writes to the repo-root `graphify-out/` that CLAUDE.md and
# git point at; narrowing it to `frontend/src` instead makes graphify write a
# second `graphify-out/` inside `frontend/src/`.
#
# Adding the backend to the graph = delete the `backend/` line. Read the note in
# CLAUDE.md first: it also pulls in ~87 documents, which cost real LLM tokens.
backend/
docs/
supabase/
changelog/
scripts/
.github/
graphify-out/
frontend/dist/
frontend/public/
frontend/coverage/

# Noise, at any depth.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
coverage/
venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.generated.py
